  <div style="margin-top: 30px;">
    <h3 style="font-size: 12pt; font-weight: bold;">What's New</h3>
    <div class="instruction">Federal tax deposits must be made by electronic funds transfer.</div>
    <div class="instruction">Beginning January 1, 2011, you must use electronic funds transfer to make all federal tax deposits (such as estimated tax, excise tax, and corporate income tax) electronically using the Electronic Federal Tax Deposit Coupon, cannot be used after December 31, 2010.</div>
  </div>

  <div style="margin-top: 20px;">
    <h3 style="font-size: 12pt; font-weight: bold;">Phone Help</h3>
    <div class="instruction">If you have questions and/or need help completing this form, please call 1-877-822-9500. This toll-free telephone service is available Monday through Friday.</div>
  </div>

  <div style="margin-top: 20px;">
    <h3 style="font-size: 12pt; font-weight: bold;">Estimated Tax Payments</h3>
    <div class="instruction">Tax-exempt corporations, tax-exempt trusts, and private foundations must make estimated tax payments if the total estimated tax for the tax year is $10,000 or more. Use Form 990-W to file the organization's estimated tax liability for 2011.</div>
  </div>

  <div style="margin-top: 20px;">
    <h3 style="font-size: 12pt; font-weight: bold;">Underpayment of Estimated Tax</h3>
    <div class="instruction">An organization that does not pay the estimated tax due when it is due may be charged an underpayment penalty under section 6655, at a rate of 20% of the unpaid amount.</div>
  </div>

  <div style="margin-top: 20px;">
    <h3 style="font-size: 12pt; font-weight: bold;">Overpayment of Estimated Tax</h3>
    <div class="instruction">An estimated tax payment may apply for a "quick refund" if the overpayment is at least 10% of its expected income tax liability for the year and is at least $500. To apply for a quick refund, complete Form 1040-X, Amended U.S. Individual Income Tax Return, and file it with your tax return.</div>
  </div>

  <div style="margin-top: 20px;">
    <h3 style="font-size: 12pt; font-weight: bold;">Electronic Deposit Requirement</h3>
    <div class="instruction">The IRS has issued final regulations under section 6302 which provide that all federal tax deposits must be made electronically.</div>
  </div>
